  "selected_best_candidate": "Candidate B (Strict Filtered Screened Poisson)",
  "honest_evaluation": "The source point cloud represents an oblique aerial forward flight where 86% of points form the dense physical river corridor (Z <= 2.5m) while 14% fan out into unprojected distant horizon/sky rays. Raw Poisson builds an artificial wedge connecting the riverbed to the sky cone and diffuses pale sky tones. Applying KD-Tree color transfer completely restores vivid natural vegetation and riverbed tones. Pruning vertices with distance > 0.03m from real points and rejecting triangles with edge > 0.07m eliminates the fabricated wedge. However, because feed-forward monocular unprojection lacks multi-view closure behind tree canopies, the dense point cloud remains the most faithful spatial representation for raw volumetric measurement, while the filtered mesh provides a clean, artifact-free surface visualization.",
